    {
      "id": "patch-differences",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Current vs Legacy (Patch Differences)",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 3,
      "paragraphs": [
        "Azmadi's difficulty has shifted across patches. Early versions dealt heavier per-hit damage and the Dash could double-hit; 0.5.2 reworked the Dash so it no longer double-hits and is used differently against melee targets.",
        "Use current footage for positioning. Legacy clips that show a double-hit Dash or fixed one-shots describe a boss that no longer exists."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "0.3.0 hotfix: lower skill damage — old one-shot claims do not apply.",
        "0.4.0c: fixed mid-fight disappearance — still verify any softlock on current patch.",
        "0.5.2: Dash no longer double-hits, melee treatment changed — rewrite positioning."
      ]
    },
